  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transatlantic Rising Stars Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Culture has been identified as a priority tool for the EU in external relations, as stated on numerous occasions by the European Commission (EC), the Council of the EU, the EU National Institutes of Culture (EUNIC) and European Parliament. Increasing the role of culture in the work of the EU Delegation to the US (EUD) directly carries forward the EC&#xbf;s recognition that cultural actors can help to strengthen international cultural relations while supporting Creative Europe&#xbf;s goal of supporting the culture and audiovisual sectors as vital contributors to our economy and social well-being. The new Transatlantic Rising Stars Project (TRSP) seeks to advance this goal while supporting the Council&#xbf;s priority of strengthening the cultural dimension of EU external relations. The EUD places a high value on the role that artists can play in opening dialogue and fostering mutual understanding. Bridging divides through our cultural actors allows us to build and maintain lasting transatlantic relations that can thrive at the grassroots level regardless of the US political context.</narrative>
  </description>
